{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>This pertains to the Levites.</b> Years disqualify [them from service] but blemishes do not disqualify among them (Sifrei; Ḥullin 24)." "<b>From twenty-five years old.</b> And in another place it says ״מִבֵּן שְׁלֹשִׁים שָׁנָה״ (Numbers 4). How so? At twenty-five he comes to learn the laws of the service and studies for five years, and at thirty he serves. From here [we learn] regarding a student who has not seen a favorable sign in his study [mastery] within five years — he will never see [it] (Sifrei; Ḥullin 24)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:01.111973253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}